NNAAMMEE
     kkggmmoonn — generate a dump of the operating system's profile buffers

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     kkggmmoonn [--bbhhpprr] [--cc _c_p_u_i_d] [--MM _c_o_r_e] [--NN _s_y_s_t_e_m]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     kkggmmoonn is a tool used when profiling the operating system.  When no argu‐
     ments are supplied, kkggmmoonn indicates the state of per-CPU operating system
     profilings as “running”, “off”, or “not configured” (see config(8)).  If
     the --pp flag is specified, kkggmmoonn extracts profile data from the operating
     system and produces a file for each CPU suitable for later analysis by
     gprof(1).

     The options are as follows:

     --bb      Resume the collection of profile data.

     --cc _c_p_u_i_d
             Operate on the CPU specified by _c_p_u_i_d, instead of all of them.

     --hh      Stop the collection of profile data.

     --MM _c_o_r_e
             Extract values associated with the name list from the specified
             _c_o_r_e instead of the default _/_d_e_v_/_k_m_e_m.

     --NN _s_y_s_t_e_m
             Extract the name list from the specified _s_y_s_t_e_m instead of the
             default _/_b_s_d.

     --pp      Dump the contents of the profile buffers into a _g_m_o_n_-_<_i_d_>_._o_u_t
             file, where “id” is the ID of the CPU.

     --rr      Reset all the profile buffers.  If the --pp flag is also specified,
             the profile files are generated before the buffers are reset.

     If neither --bb nor --hh is specified, the state of profiling collection re‐
     mains unchanged.  For example, if the --pp flag is specified and profile
     data is being collected, profiling will be momentarily suspended, the op‐
     erating system profile buffers will be dumped, and profiling will be im‐
     mediately resumed.

     kkggmmoonn requires the ability to open _/_d_e_v_/_k_m_e_m which may be restricted
     based upon the value of the _k_e_r_n_._a_l_l_o_w_k_m_e_m sysctl(8).

FFIILLEESS
     /bsd        default system
     /dev/kmem   default memory

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     Users with only read permission on _/_d_e_v_/_k_m_e_m cannot change the state of
     profiling collection.  They can get profile files with the warning that
     the data may be inconsistent if profiling is in progress.

